# Docker build context allowlist for the Fly API image (built from the
# repo root; see server/Dockerfile). The image needs the server app, the
# shared data/ tables, and the vendored planner submodule; everything
# else (frontend, git history, reference assets) is excluded to keep the
# remote build context small and fast to upload.
*
!server
!data
# Re-include the vendored planner submodule. server/game/planner-graph.js
# reads vendor/hf-mission-planner/assets/data-hf4.json at boot to build
# the ~1500-node movement graph, and server/Dockerfile COPYs vendor/.
# Without this the allowlist above strips vendor/ from the context and the
# COPY fails with "/vendor: not found". The submodule must also be checked
# out for the file to exist on disk (deploy-api uses submodules: recursive).
!vendor

# Re-exclude things that live under the allowed dirs but must not ship.
# Drop the parts of the planner submodule that aren't needed at runtime
# (docs, prebuilt dist, source, type stubs, git + node tooling) to keep
# the context lean. assets/ stays because it holds data-hf4.json. These
# are plain directory excludes, the same mechanism as server/node_modules.
vendor/hf-mission-planner/.git
vendor/hf-mission-planner/.github
vendor/hf-mission-planner/docs
vendor/hf-mission-planner/dist
vendor/hf-mission-planner/src
vendor/hf-mission-planner/types
vendor/hf-mission-planner/node_modules
server/node_modules
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.log
.env
